From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Droidspaces-OKI <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: preserve 6.12.23 KMI when enabling PIDS

Target: Android GKI android16-6.12-2025-06 and OnePlus 15 6.12.23
Frozen configuration: CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=n

Keep the frozen subsystem IDs, public cgroup/css_set arrays and all
Android KABI/backport reserves unchanged. Append only PIDS to the runtime
controller table and use a separate active count for iteration, masks,
hashing, migration and cgroup.stat.

Store the PIDS state, cset links and 6.12 dying-CSS counter in private
allocation tails. Dynamic css_sets, cgroup roots and non-root cgroups
allocate their extension together with the owner, so allocation failures,
error cleanup and RCU teardown share the existing lifetime. Static boot
objects use separate static storage. Place non-root extensions after the
full ancestors[] allocation and initialize root/level before housekeeping.

Adapt the cgroup access helpers from the FullDocker implementation in
superturtlee/kernel-workshop-docker.
Use the private-tail KMI approach from the sibling 6.1/6.6 limits patches.
Module symbol version checking is retained.

Enable CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y in the target kernel configuration separately.
CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH=y is already supported by these 6.12 target trees.
Other controller options must match the frozen vendor configuration.
This patch targets a KMI frozen with PIDS disabled.

Usage from the common kernel source directory:
    patch -p1 < fix_cgroup_limits_kabi_6.12.23.patch

Link: https://github.com/cctv18/android_gki_kernel_common/commit/9e91eb74a201e8cee839c8db6d642ff9b8408388
Link: https://github.com/cctv18/android_kernel_common_oneplus_sm8850/commit/1fdec1073c8fa24282dcbe8395593759c2ce0d17
Link: https://github.com/superturtlee/kernel-workshop-docker/tree/31ec2d1d36bf448c84b133ff0a24137eb4bafb11

